  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 323 PM EDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\n===== Friday through the Weekend =====\n\nThe upper ridge will begin to build back to the west on Friday as \nupper troughing deepens over the northeast. This will result in a \nweak backdoor cold front to approach the region from the northeast \nsometime on Friday. We'll see an uptick in moisture advection on \nFriday, and perhaps some isolated to scattered showers and/or \nstorms, especially for the Bluegrass region. We'll still be dealing \nwith the heat then too, with forecast highs in the upper 90s, and \nsfc dewpoints creeping up into the mid-70s. Heat indices around \nabove 100F are likely across the entire forecast area. The heat \nadvisory will probably need to be extended into Friday too, but with \na chance for PoPs, it makes the confidence a little lower. \n\nHigher precip chances arrive on Saturday as that cold front sweeps \ninto the forecast area. Thunderstorms will be possible Saturday \nafternoon and evening. Long range deterministic soundings show steep \nlow level lapse rates and an uncapped profile, but weaker shear \nparameters could help keep storms unorganized. The wind profiles will \nbe rather weak, with less than 20kts below 500 mb. We'll begin to \nsee temps transition back to the 80s on Sunday, with split temps \nbetween the upper 80s in our east and lower 90s in our west.",
